From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:45:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] d3d12: enhanced barriers, ID3D12Device9 and 10

OPTIONS12 reports EnhancedBarriersSupported. A Barrier call is one
ResourceBarrier call of the legacy barriers its groups mean to DXMT, which
orders whole encoders (d3d12_barrier_legacy.hpp, header-only so the VM's guest
forwarder translates with it too): nothing to wait on (SyncBefore NONE, no
access before, a global read) is nothing; a texture or buffer barrier is a
transition between its accesses' legacy states (UAV to UAV a UAV barrier; an
access with no legacy state, or a global write, a barrier naming any
resource); sync stages, layouts, ranges and DISCARD change nothing.

The device is ID3D12Device10: CreateCommandQueue1 is CreateCommandQueue, the
shader cache controls answer E_NOTIMPL, CreateCommittedResource3 and
CreatePlacedResource2 take their initial layout as a state (an upload heap's
GENERIC_READ, a readback's COPY_DEST) and ignore castable formats (warned once;
RelaxedFormatCastingSupported stays FALSE); CreateReservedResource2 answers
E_NOTIMPL as CreateReservedResource1 does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
